{"title":"NYT debate on the rules for AI companies","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/972012611/0/marginalrevolution~NYT-debate-on-the-rules-for-AI-companies.html","date":1793089078000,"content":"<p>Emily Bazelon was the moderator, there were five of us in <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/26/magazine/ai-companies-law-regulations.html?smid=nytcore-ios-share\" target=\"_blank\">the symposium</a>.  Excerpt from me:</p>\r\n<blockquote>\r\n<p><strong>Bores: </strong>Do you think the federal government pre-empting the states is consistent with democracy?</p>\r\n<p><strong>Cowen: </strong>Absolutely. We have federal laws that pre-empt state lawmaking in many other areas. Courts have upheld it many, many times.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Bores: </strong>OK, but is it pro-democracy, in giving people a say?</p>\r\n<p><strong>Cowen: </strong>It is pro-American Constitution.</p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n<p>Most of the panel disagreed with most of my points.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/10/nyt-debate-on-the-rules-for-ai-companies.html\">NYT debate on the rules for AI companies</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/972012611/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/972012611/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/972012611/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/972012611/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.c